 "description": "Gaze heads on a vision-language checkpoint (Gandikota and Bau, 2026), on the tiny Qwen3-VL: each row's image is two halves, red|blue or blue|red, and the question asks for the colour on one side; `left` is that side's box on the row and `right` the other's. `gaze` reads every head's attention from the last prompt token to the asked side's image tokens (`select key` names the keys by a region of the image) and `rest` to the other side's; `score` is each head's mean mass on the asked side, the gaze score, and `whole` checks that the two masses sum to the mass on the image. `steered` then biases heads 0 and 2 of block 1 toward the OTHER side by +10000 on its keys and -10000 on the asked side's, in the prefill and at every decode call, so those heads look only there; `null` biases them by 0, which equals `plain` to the bit. The model block's `task` loads the checkpoint with its processor, which an image part needs, and `attn_implementation: eager` serves the attention interior.",
